        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Siegi Sessler, Bette Davis, Frank Sinatra, Humphrey Bogart, Bob Hope, Bing Crosby, David Niven, Marlon Brando, Marilyn Monroe, John Wayne, Cary Grant, Clark Gable, Doris Day, Joan Crawford, Ingrid Bergman, Elizabeth Taylor\n- Places: a Hollywood stars' gathering place\n- Topics: celebrity patronage, acting\n\nFacts:\n- A place associated with Siegi Sessler was well known as a \"home away from home\" for Hollywood stars.\n- The Hollywood stars said to frequent that place included Frank Sinatra, Humphrey Bogart, Bob Hope, Bing Crosby, David Niven, Marlon Brando, Marilyn Monroe, John Wayne, Cary Grant, Bette Davis, Clark Gable, Doris Day, Joan Crawford, Ingrid Bergman, and Elizabeth Taylor.\n- Ruth Elizabeth \"Bette\" Davis was born on April 5, 1908.\n- Bette Davis was an American actress of film, television, and theater with Welsh ancestry.\n- Bette Davis died on October 6, 1989.",
